 "▼ Dive in: <0>Five parts</0>": "",
 "An <0>agent</0> is not a new kind of model. It is an ordinary LLM wrapped in a <1>loop</1> that can call <2>tools</2>, keeps <3>memory</3> (the context), and works toward a <4>goal</4>.": "",
 "The model only ever does one thing: predict the next token. The loop around it turns that into behaviour.": "",
 "The code around the model is called the <0>harness</0> (or runtime / scaffold). It is plain software: it parses, executes, appends and decides when to stop.": "",
 "Memory has layers: the context window (short-term) plus anything the harness stores outside and re-injects (files, databases, retrieval).": "",
 "goal / user request": "",
 "context (messages)": "",
 "done?": "",
 "The task, stated in the user message (and the system prompt). The model has no goals of its own: the goal is just <0>text in the context</0>.": "",
 "The frozen network. It reads the whole context and emits tokens: either prose or a structured tool call. See <0>autoregressive loop</0>.": "",
 "Ordinary functions (search, run code, book a table). The model never runs them; it only <0>asks</0>, in JSON. See <1>tool definitions</1>.": "",
 "Short-term: the messages so far (the context window). Long-term: files, databases, vector stores that the harness reads and writes. See <0>memory types</0>.": "",
 "The harness: call model, check <0/>, execute tool calls, append results, repeat. Also enforces budgets. See the loop on the <1>agent loop slide</1>.": "",
