 "▼ Dive in: <0>Same task, {#} ways</0>": "",
 "The dividing line is <0>who decides what happens next</0>: you (code), or the model.": "",
 "A chatbot answers once. A workflow follows a path you wrote. An agent chooses its own steps at runtime.": "",
 "More autonomy buys flexibility on open-ended tasks but costs predictability, latency, tokens and safety margin. A common recommendation is to use the simplest pattern that works.": "",
 "Real systems mix them: a fixed workflow with one agentic step inside.": "",
