 "<0>{#}</0> Tokens spell a JSON tool call": "",
 "<0/> <1/> After many forward passes, the generated tokens decode to text that is valid JSON. Nothing magic: the model learned to emit this format.": "",
 "<0>{#}</0> Harness executes (ordinary code)": "",
 "<0/> <1/> The harness parses the JSON, looks the name up in a registry and <2>calls a real function</2>. No neural network involved.": "",
 "<0>{#}</0> Result → appended tokens": "",
 "<0/> <1/> The result is wrapped in a message, serialized by the template and tokenized into new <2/> <3/> IDs appended to the sequence. Then the model predicts again.": "",
 "The agent is <0>a loop around repeated next-token prediction</0>.": "",
 "Outer loop (harness, ordinary code):": "",
 "one iteration per tool round-trip - typically a handful, bounded by a max-iteration limit.": "",
 "<0>Inner loop (decoding):</0> one iteration per generated token - dozens for a tool call, hundreds for an answer. Each iteration = forward pass → logits → sample → append token (<1>details</1>).": "",
 "Why the loop helps: the model's own output (a tool call) and the tool's result land back in the context where attention can read them. Compare with chain-of-thought as a scratchpad in <0>reasoning</0>. See the protocol side in <1>the tool round-trip</1>.": "",
